meta {
  name: kyc-onboarding-status
}

docs {
  # KYC verification advances the fleet owner's onboarding status (BUG-108)

  `users.onboarding_status` of a fleet owner (TORG_ADMIN) is derived server-side
  (`OnboardingStatusService`). Ladder: BASIC_DETAILS_ADDED -> BUSINESS_DETAILS_ADDED (primary PAN
  and Aadhaar both exist for the torg) -> ONBOARDING_COMPLETED (both VERIFIED). It never regresses.

  Before BUG-108 the status was only recomputed when the app sent a user update. A PAN or Aadhaar
  that an admin verified afterwards left the owner stuck at BUSINESS_DETAILS_ADDED. Now
  `PANCardService` (create, `PUT /api/pan/{id}/verify`, `PUT /api/pan/{id}/retry-verification`),
  `AadhaarService.updateAadhaar` (`PUT /api/aadhaar/{id}/verify`) and `DigilockerService` call
  `recomputeForTorg` when a document becomes VERIFIED.

  Needs the static VAHN_ADMIN token from plutus-java `config.yml`
  (`auth.static_tokens.role_tokens.VAHN_ADMIN`). Pass it on the command line so it never lands in a file:

      npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/flows/plutus-api/kyc-onboarding-status --env staging \
        --env-var adminStaticToken="$TOKEN"

  Steps (each run creates a brand new owner with a random phone, a random PAN and a random Aadhaar,
  OTP `667766`; nothing moves money or sends messages beyond the staging OTP login):

  - 1-3: new user, becomes TORG_ADMIN with a name (torg auto-created), re-login for a TORG_ADMIN token.
  - 4-5: owner adds PAN (`POST /api/pan`, tries Surepass through Surepass, may stay PENDING) and
    Aadhaar (`POST /api/aadhaar`, always PENDING).
  - 6: the app's last onboarding update -> BUSINESS_DETAILS_ADDED.
  - 7: admin verifies the PAN (skipped when staging already auto-verified it).
  - 8: status must still be BUSINESS_DETAILS_ADDED (Aadhaar pending).
  - 9: admin verifies the Aadhaar.
  - 10: admin reads the user: ONBOARDING_COMPLETED with no further app user-update call. This is the
    BUG-108 check.

  Not covered: `GET /api/v1/digilocker/status` needs a real DigiLocker session.
  All state is kept in runtime vars (`bru.setVar`), so nothing is written to `environments/`.
}
